    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed"><strong>Status.</strong> This paper states a thesis, hypotheses, falsifiers and a programme of work; the results it reports are the Phase 0 measurements that need no learned proposer (the Form corpus, the name-free Form space, the determinism streams and the adversarial Forms, in the Status section), and no result for a learned proposer is reported because none has been trained. JEPA is the premise: predict a summary of meaning, not the surface text. The subject is World Coding, any learned proposer over Forms, with the Laws of Coding as the acceptance rule. The survey later on this page is building-phase reading, not a measured proposer result. The deciding half (commit gate, exact replay, projection, and cost counted in integer units with energy estimates labelled <code>est_j</code>) is described in <a href="/papers/rce/">the RCE paper</a>; this paper is about the proposer: a learned model that steers search over Forms while the engine renders every target. Any model in the loop, hosted or local, only proposes, and security never depends on it.</p>

