    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">In plain words</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>The subject is World Coding. A World of Code is the space of program Forms, plus exact rules for the next state and for what is accepted (the Laws of Coding). JEPA is the premise, not the whole method: predict a summary of meaning instead of the next word of code. AI (artificial intelligence) here means any learned proposer, not one architecture.</li>
        <li>The model proposes and the checker decides. Trace-trained decoders, diffusion, reinforcement learning inside a proof checker, evolutionary search, library learning and constrained decoding can all sit in that slot. The gate does not change when the proposer does. Safety does not depend on the proposer being right.</li>
        <li>Measured floors stay labeled, and unfinished work stays unfinished. On hand-written programs the median description-length ratio is 9.34 over 185 programs. A fuzzed check found 0 broken invariants in 1,275 accepted mutants. Replay matched on 10,500 streams across six targets. A deterministic ladder closed 111 of 151 tasks (73.5%) with zero model calls and left 40. No learned proposer has been trained, and the comparison of proposer types on those 40 tasks at equal energy has no result. Energy is electricity in joules. This page explains the unit and does not invent a joule count.</li>
      </ol>
