    <h2 id="principles">Principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The model only proposes.</li>
      <li>The checker decides.</li>
      <li>Security never depends on the model.</li>
      <li>No model runs inside the Reality Code Engine's own toolchain loop.</li>
      <li>Every accepted program form is replayable bit for bit.</li>
      <li>Any decision model, hosted or local, is only a proposer outside the gate.</li>
      <li>Deterministic first. The first rule of automation is having a manual process that works: a ladder of exact, deterministic proposers runs before any model, and the model acts only on what that ladder leaves open (stated in the proposer section below).</li>
    </ul>

