    <p><strong>Lane reading.</strong> Each of these hybrids has the shape stated in the principles above: the model proposes, and a deterministic gate decides. AlphaEvolve and AlphaProof are clear points of contact. The Lean provers are the same shape with the kernel as the gate, and the gains they report came from data generated against that kernel. The ARC Prize 2025 page shows program search, test-time training, diffusion and small recursive nets on one loop: propose, check against examples, refine. The shared limit is also shared. They need an evaluator, a kernel, or a set of examples. The Laws of Coding are the claim that an environment of that kind exists for coding in general, not only for mathematics and for benchmark kernels. Large Concept Models are the closest token-free relative of JEPA in language: prediction in a concept space, still without an exact acceptance step.</p>

    <h3 id="lane-formula">3.3 Reconceptions of computation, programming and coding</h3>
    <p>This lane does not start from a benchmark score. It starts from a question about what a program is.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-xs border-collapse [&_td]:border [&_th]:border [&_td]:border-brand-border [&_th]:border-brand-border [&_td]:p-2 [&_th]:p-2 [&_th]:text-left [&_th]:text-brand-white [&_td]:align-top">
      <thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>As reported</th><th>Unfinished in that source</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>HVM2, Higher Order Company</td><td>Interaction combinators as a model of computation, with parallelism inherent in the model. This page cites the model.</td><td>Figures in that paper are not used here. Production adoption is open.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Unison [C2]</td><td>A definition is the hash of its syntax tree. Names are views over that hash. The language is in production use.</td><td>Ecosystem size.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lean, Dafny and Verus communities, via the vericoding benchmark [C34]</td><td>A proof is a program the kernel can check. Correctness is a checkable object. The measured floor used here is the vericoding row above.</td><td>The cost of writing the specification remains.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>egg [C4]</td><td>Program equivalence classes as data. Programs live in a quotient.</td><td>Completeness of the rewrite rules.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lean FRO (Focused Research Organization), Year 1 roadmap, August 2023 to July 2024</td><td>Lean as a language and a proof assistant for mathematics and for software and hardware verification. The deliverables named on that page include a standard library, a module system, Lake and Reservoir, proof automation, machine-learning integration and a new code generator.</td><td>Later-year roadmaps are not used on this page.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Conal Elliott, denotational design</td><td>"The instance's meaning is the meaning's instance." A semantic model defines correctness and carries it to the implementation. The note is from 2009, revised 2016.</td><td>A manual design discipline.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Radul and Sussman, propagators</td><td>Computation as autonomous machines that add information to shared cells. The account unifies expression-style programming and constraint programming, including incremental distributed search. A 2009 technical report, with a Scheme implementation.</td><td>Adoption.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Chollet, on the measure of intelligence [T37]</td><td>Intelligence as skill-acquisition efficiency. ARC is the measure. Program synthesis is the framing. The 2019 paper is the citation. Later talks on synthesis done at the moment of the task are not cited on their own. Where the ARC Prize 2024 report names deep-learning-guided program synthesis, that report is the citation.</td><td>The formal measure is not operationalized beyond ARC in the abstract read for this lane.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>This project, the Laws of Coding</td><td>A canonical Form is the object. Surface text is a projection. Cost is counted. Measured floors, left exact: H1 median rho 9.34 over 185 programs; H7, 1,275 mutants and 0 violations on the fuzzed arm; H8, 10,500 streams, six targets, 0 mismatches; H14 run 3, 111 of 151 (73.5%) closed with zero model calls.</td><td>The learned proposer is not trained. H2 to H6 and H9 to H13 are open. H15 is unfinished. The residual after H14 run 3 is 40 tasks.</td></tr>
