        <tr><td>Reinforcement learning in a formal environment</td><td>Steps that a kernel accepts, as in AlphaProof and the Lean provers of Section 3</td><td>The kernel is the environment. For software, that role is the checker</td><td>In the reports read here the domain is mathematics, not software. Compute cost is part of the AlphaProof result. Goedel-Prover version 1 has no reinforcement learning</td><td>H3 and H12, if the same loop is run on Forms. Not a result</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Evolutionary search</td><td>Edits, kept or dropped by an evaluator, as in AlphaEvolve and in SOAR on the ARC Prize 2025 page</td><td>An evaluator. Here the evaluator is the checker, not a test suite alone</td><td>The loop works where an evaluator exists. Example checks, as on ARC, are not a general acceptance rule for software</td><td>The evolutionary arm of H15, on the residual of H14</td></tr>
